Modelica source:
```modelica
connector Pin
  Real v;
  flow Real i;
end Pin;
model Ports0
  Pin flange;
end Ports0;
model Ports1
  Pin flange;
  Pin support;
end Ports1;
model Ports2
  Pin flange_a;
  Pin flange_b;
end Ports2;
model Ports3
  Pin flange_a;
  Pin flange_b;
  Pin support;
end Ports3;
model Study
  Ports2 Inertia1;
  Ports2 Inertia2;
  Ports3 bearingFriction;
  Ports0 fixed;
  Ports3 gear;
  Ports1 torque1;
  Ports1 torque2;
equation
  connect(torque2.flange, Inertia2.flange_b);
  connect(Inertia2.flange_a, gear.flange_b);
  connect(gear.flange_a, Inertia1.flange_b);
  connect(Inertia1.flange_a, bearingFriction.flange_b);
  connect(bearingFriction.flange_a, torque1.flange);
  connect(gear.support, fixed.flange);
  connect(fixed.flange, torque2.support);
  connect(fixed.flange, bearingFriction.support);
  connect(torque1.support, fixed.flange);
end Study;
```

Question:
Return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set containing bearingFriction.support.i.

Target:
bearingFriction.support.i

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
